WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.741 --> 00:00:05.401
- I essentially don't have a pulse.

00:00:05.401 --> 00:00:06.882
You can check everywhere you'd want

00:00:06.882 --> 00:00:08.530
and you won't feel a pulse.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.955
So I'm pretty much the best
looking zombie you'll ever see.

00:00:11.955 --> 00:00:14.038
(laughs)

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.141
My name is Andrew Jones
and I'm a professional

00:00:19.141 --> 00:00:22.648
fitness model, living
with an artificial heart.

00:00:22.648 --> 00:00:24.841
I always have to have batteries charging.

00:00:24.841 --> 00:00:26.729
At night when I'm going to
bed, I'll plug my phone in

00:00:26.729 --> 00:00:29.942
and then I'll plug myself
into the wall outlet

00:00:29.942 --> 00:00:32.942
to make sure I have power overnight.

00:00:37.544 --> 00:00:40.915
In 2012, I was diagnosed
with a cardiomyopathy

00:00:40.915 --> 00:00:45.379
which affects the heart’s
efficiency to pump blood.

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:48.026
I was incredibly ill at the time

00:00:48.026 --> 00:00:51.607
and I was admitted to
the ICU for four months

00:00:51.607 --> 00:00:55.230
where they had to implant
what's called an LVAD,

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:58.415
which stands for Left
Ventricular Assist Device.

00:00:58.415 --> 00:01:01.346
And it's considered an artificial heart.

00:01:01.346 --> 00:01:04.603
It's taking over the
work of my heart for me.

00:01:04.603 --> 00:01:08.276
These devices, the two
batteries and the computer,

00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:11.005
these are what are
powering and controlling

00:01:11.005 --> 00:01:13.066
the artificial heart, to make sure that

00:01:13.066 --> 00:01:17.681
it's working efficiently
and working properly.

00:01:17.681 --> 00:01:20.685
I started feeling strong
again when I was recovering

00:01:20.685 --> 00:01:24.146
after having the
artificial heart implanted.

00:01:24.146 --> 00:01:26.909
And, of course, it didn't all
come at once, I took baby steps

00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:31.230
and I found myself back in
the gym sooner than later.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:35.064
And I got my strength back
and once I'm able to find

00:01:35.064 --> 00:01:37.664
the right match for a heart transplant,

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:40.341
I'll no longer need my artificial heart.

00:01:40.341 --> 00:01:42.942
At first I was upset about
having an artificial heart

00:01:42.942 --> 00:01:45.290
and then there was the
moment where I realized that

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:49.123
this is my life for now
and either I can dwell

00:01:50.112 --> 00:01:54.359
and feel sorry for myself, or I
can continue doing the things

00:01:54.359 --> 00:01:58.482
that I love to do, the best way
I can and I haven't stopped.

00:01:58.482 --> 00:02:01.409
I'm proud of the scars that
I have from my surgeries

00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:04.789
because scars are beautiful,
they're a part of you.

00:02:04.789 --> 00:02:08.956
They tell your story and no one
can take that away from you.

00:02:10.811 --> 00:02:13.478
(heart beating)

